# MkDocs build output. Cloudflare Pages rebuilds this from source on every push
# to main (see doc/help/DEPLOYMENT.md), so the committed copy served no purpose
# beyond going stale and swamping every docs diff.
doc/help/site/
# AI tooling
# Shared agent rules live in AGENTS.md and shared skills in .agents/skills/ (both
# committed). .claude/skills/ holds committed symlinks to them; the rest of each
# tool's folder, and CLAUDE.local.md, stays local.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.codex/
.grok/
.playwright-mcp/
# Translation state. The docs manifest is what detects "English changed, so
# fr/de/es are now stale", so it has to be shared — the translate-docs skill
# already documents it as committed. The app-locale manifest stays local.
# Note: the glob must be /translation-state/* rather than translation-state/,
# because git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded. That
# anchors it to the repo root, so nested copies need their own rule.
**/translation-state/
!/translation-state/
/translation-state/*
!/translation-state/docs-source-hashes.json
/tasks/
